{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1218291-bloodline-idea-the-chronara","id":1218291,"title":"Bloodline IDEA - the Chronara","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-13T12:09:07-07:00","id":1218291,"title":"Bloodline IDEA - the Chronara","content":"Just an idea I had while out on my daily walk. Won't commit to much time to it (at least not right now or anytime soon), but thought it could be something people may want to develop as a possible new Bloodline.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Auspex, Celerity, <i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate<br /> <b>Weakness</b>: Mekhet Bane; and maybe something to do with frenzy regarding lateness (being late, being made to wait, people not being on time EXACTLY [i.e.: not a second too soon OR late])<br /> <br /> <b>Personality</b>: The Chronara are an arrogant bunch. Many would think them Ventrue given their arrogance and snobishness (leading partial from Dominate being their Bloodline favored discipline; making anyone arrogant). Their arrogance however comes from a unique perspective however. The Chronara are impaitent, so much so that even the ETERNITY of an Immortal is not forever. The final death is always coming, and there is much work to do before that happens. SOO much to do!<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b>: Lost to history. They are an old Bloodline. Hard to pick HOW old (bloody obfuscate AND Dominate Mind wipes!!), but its suspected they are of Greek Origins - taking their name from the God of Time &quot;Chronos&quot;; though equally from the leader of the Titans Cronos father of Zeus (the devouring of children to spawn a pantheon could be mis-interpreted as an &quot;embrace&quot;). The commanding element of Dominate also fits into the idea of Vampires playing &quot;the children of Greek Gods&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Devotions</b>: I prefer my custom Bloodlines to be more &quot;Devotion&quot; based rather than &quot;here's a 4th Discipline&quot; as it lends to Kindred feeling more 'related'. It also gives nice justification to why (in 2nd Ed) a Mehket can start with a dot in Dominate without needing a backstory connecting them to a Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Anyway the suggested Chronara Devotions revolve around &quot;Time Manipulation&quot; which is achieved through a mix of super human speed and senses (Celerity + Auspex) while dampening sensory and motor responses (i.e.: using Dominate to &quot;command&quot; victims to move slower). As such ALL Disciplines require a use of ALL three abilities (as the effects are powerful, requiring extra training to achieve).<br /> <br /> At the LOWER levels, the &quot;Freeze&quot; command is a bit more global - meaning ALL targets are hit by it (friend or foe) - which works well for the theme of slowing time (if everyone is affected, its harder to notice). <br /> <br /> Some tricks they can pull off:<ul><li>Subliminal Command - using Celerity to speak inhumanly fast, and Obfuscate to hide EVEN those small motions, the Kindred commands a quick &quot;one-word&quot; command to a target (very commonly &quot;Freeze&quot;). This is essentially the first level use of Dominate, but with the added effect it appears to happen silently - making it a powerful espionage tool.</li> </ul><ul><li>Teleport - in a MICRO-second, they go invisible, give a command to freeze, use Celerity to re-position themselves in that brief moment of freeze, and reappear as the act of &quot;attacking&quot; breaks the obfuscate effect. Still allows for backstabbing and improved escapes.</li> </ul><ul><li>Sudden Changes (same Disciplines as teleport but with HIGHER Obfuscate) - Vampire Teleports as above to repostion objects; the higher obfuscate allowing</li> </ul><ul><li>Sudden Injuries (same Disciplines as teleport but with HIGHER Obfuscate AND Dominate) - Vampire Teleports as above to attack a target, but contains the hidden state better, AND through Dominate makes the target forget they were attacked. Resulting in the victim suffering a spontaneous injury. If the Vampire resumes their original position, they become harder to recognize as the cause of the attack.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Anyway that was my brainstorm. If anyone thinks this has merit, I'd be curious to see what you would devise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}